        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-negation-bu-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Say what is not true",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put 不 before a verb or quality for a general negative statement. With 是, use 不是. This does not describe an action that failed to happen in the past.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我不学中文。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bù xué Zhōngwén 。",
                "meaning": "I do not study Chinese.",
                "audio": "3a4ad76ae35c88f377163ea231906ab0565d00fa95e4c2174e59325818db2605"
              },
              {
                "text": "不是她，是他。",
                "pinyin": "bù shì tā ， shì tā 。",
                "meaning": "It is not her; it is him.",
